message:
Now I can see the exact bug. In the XML case (line ~1000):
```c
} else if(encoding == UA_EXTENSIONOBJECT_ENCODED_XML) {
    dst->encoding = (UA_ExtensionObjectEncoding)encoding;
    dst->content.encoded.typeId = binTypeId; /* move to dst */
    ret = ByteString_decodeBinary(&dst->content.encoded.body);
    if(ret != UA_STATUSCODE_GOOD)
        UA_NodeId_deleteMembers(&dst->content.encoded.typeId);
}
```

When `ByteString_decodeBinary` fails, it frees `dst->content.encoded.typeId` but leaves `dst->encoding` as XML. Then when `Array_decodeBinary` calls `UA_Array_delete` → `ExtensionObject_deleteMembers`, it will free `typeId` again → double-free.

Now let me look at `Array_decodeBinary` and `ExtensionObject_deleteMembers`:

<｜｜DSML｜｜r>
